  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><strong>Effective date:</strong> September 29, 2026</p>

  <p class="notice">
    Before publishing this policy, replace <strong>pyty639504@gmail.com</strong>
    with a monitored email address.
  </p>

  <p>
    This Privacy Policy describes how the Threads Account Analysis Tool
    ("the Tool") collects, uses, stores, and deletes information.
  </p>

  <h2>Information the Tool processes</h2>
  <p>The Tool may process:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Public Threads usernames and public profile information.</li>
    <li>Public Threads posts and associated public metadata, including post text, timestamps, links, media metadata, topic tags, and public interaction counts when provided by the Threads API.</li>
    <li>Authentication information supplied by an authorized Tool operator, including a Threads API access token.</li>
    <li>Operational information needed to diagnose API errors and complete requested exports.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How information is used</h2>
  <p>
    Information is used to retrieve public Threads content requested by an
    authorized operator, organize that content, perform content and activity
    analysis, and create local reports or spreadsheet exports.
  </p>

  <h2>Data sharing and sale</h2>
  <p>
    The Tool does not sell personal information. Information is not shared
    with third parties except as necessary to operate services selected by the
    authorized operator or as required by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Storage and security</h2>
  <p>
    Retrieved information and API responses may be stored locally by the
    authorized operator. Reasonable measures are used to protect access
    credentials and collected information. Access tokens are not intentionally
    included in spreadsheet exports.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Information is retained only as long as needed for the requested analysis
    or as required by applicable law. The authorized operator controls local
    report and raw-response retention.
  </p>

  <h2>Data deletion</h2>
  <p>
    To request deletion of information associated with use of the Tool, email
    <strong>pyty639504@gmail.com</strong>. Requests will be reviewed and
    completed where applicable. Authorized operators may also delete locally
    stored workbooks and raw API-response files directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The Tool uses the Meta Threads API. Meta's own terms and privacy policies
    apply to information processed by Meta.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may be updated to reflect changes to the Tool or applicable
    requirements. The effective date above will be updated when material
    changes are made.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Email: <strong>pyty639504@gmail.com</strong></p>
